{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the problem and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned status 200.\n\n**Root cause:** `product-catalog` couldn't log in to Postgres as `otelu`, because the database rejected the password. The connection string in the `product-catalog-db-conn` secret matched `postgresql-init`, so the role's stored password had to be wrong. Product lookups failed, which showed up as `Product Not Found` errors in the frontend and failed product loads in `recommendation`.\n\n**Fix:** I reset the password with `ALTER USER otelu WITH PASSWORD '…'`, using the value from the secret. I then restarted `product-catalog`.\n\n**Checks:** Postgres has logged no new `otelu` authentication failures since the fix, and `otelu` has the privileges it needs on the `catalog` schema. I didn't re-test product pages end to end.\n\nAll the feature flags in the flagd config were already `off`, so none of them was the cause."}}
